<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Invisible track for the fast scroller (see FastScrollerHelper). Replaces AndroidFastScroll's
    afs_md2_track, which draws a full-height 8dp bar down the edge of the list.

    ⚠️ TRANSPARENT, NOT ABSENT - and it must stay a <shape> with an explicit <size>.

    1. The track cannot be removed. FastScroller.onTouchEvent hit-tests mThumbView first (-> drag),
       then falls through to mTrackView (-> scrollToThumbOffset + setDragging), so the track IS the
       tap-to-jump target. Drop it and you lose tap-to-jump; pass null and getIntrinsicWidth() NPEs.

    2. It cannot be a ColorDrawable. The FastScroller constructor runs
           requireNonNegative(trackDrawable.getIntrinsicWidth(), "trackDrawable.getIntrinsicWidth() < 0")
       and ColorDrawable's intrinsic width is -1, so setTrackDrawable(ColorDrawable(TRANSPARENT))
       throws IllegalArgumentException at build time - on every list at once. The explicit <size>
       below is what makes the intrinsic width valid.

    Width stays 8dp to match afs_md2_track, because mTrackWidth feeds the scroller's layout and the
    thumb is positioned against it. Height is deliberately unset (intrinsic height -1 is fine here -
    only the track's WIDTH is range-checked, and afs_md2_track omits height too).

    NOTE ON TOUCH: making this invisible does NOT change hit-testing. FastScroller.onTouchEvent is
    gated on mScrollbarEnabled, which updateScrollbarState sets purely from `getScrollOffsetRange() > 0`
    - i.e. "is this list scrollable". Auto-hide only fades the views; the flag stays true. So the
    ~48dp live zone along the edge (isInTouchTarget expands to afs_min_touch_target_size) is present
    on every scrollable list already, with or without this file. See FastScrollerHelper for the
    escape hatch if that ever needs reducing.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">

    <size android:width="8dp" />

    <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />

</shape>
